+# LED-105: Revenue endpoint
+
+## Ticket
+LED-105 · Finance wants revenue over HTTP: `GET /reports/revenue?currency=EUR`.
+
+## Summary
+- New `GET /reports/revenue?currency=…` (defaults to USD) returns `{currency, total_cents, invoice_count}` for paid invoices.
+- Conversion goes through `payments.fx.convert` on integer cents; the float-based `services/reports.py` is untouched.
+- New `services/revenue.py` holds the logic; `api/routes_reports.py` only maps HTTP.
+
+## ADRs touched
+- ADR-0001 money as integer cents: amounts stay `Money`, converted with `fx.convert`, no floats.
+- ADR-0002 layered architecture: new route → new service → existing repo; no api → repo import.
+
+## Verification
+| gate | command | result | detail |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| tests | `uv run pytest -q` | ✅ pass | 22 passed, 1 deselected in 0.16s |
+| lint | `uv run ruff check .` | ✅ pass | All checks passed! |
+| format | `uv run ruff format --check .` | ✅ pass | 32 files already formatted |
+| architecture | `uv run lint-imports` | ✅ pass | Contracts: 2 kept, 0 broken. |
+
+4/4 gates green.
+
+## Risk & rollback
+- Risk: rounding in multi-currency totals differs from the legacy report (by design, half-even). Finance should expect it.
+- Rollback: additive endpoint, no migration. Revert the commit.
+
+## Changelog
+- 2026-10-19 GET /reports/revenue — revenue of paid invoices in any supported currency
